# The build context is url-fetcher/, and devserver.py is the ONE file in it that constructs a
# guard permitting loopback origins. Excluding it here is half of what makes
# "a manifest cannot produce the permissive construction" a property rather than a sentence:
# the file is not in the context, so no COPY in the Dockerfile can ship it by accident and no
# `command:` can reach it in the image. build-checks.py copies the WHOLE context into the
# builder stage and fails the build if it finds devserver.py there, so deleting this line
# fails the build rather than quietly shipping the file.
devserver.py

# build artefacts of a local run; the image compiles nothing and writes nothing
__pycache__
